---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Every file-processing tool on Creek Mechanical runs entirely in your browser. Files are never uploaded to a server."
>
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Your files never leave your browser.</strong> Every CAD viewer,
      converter, and analysis tool on this site processes your files
      entirely on your own device, using WebAssembly running locally in
      your browser tab. We never receive, store, or have access to any file
      you open, convert, or check with these tools — there is no upload
      step, because there is no server for a file to be uploaded to.
    </div>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics (GA4) to count visits and see which pages and
      tools people actually use. It runs on every page of this site, sets
      cookies in your browser, and sends Google your IP address, approximate
      location, device and browser details, and the pages you view. Google
      processes that data on our behalf and under their own terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is the only tracking on this site, and it is the only thing that
      leaves your browser. It measures pages, not files: the CAD viewer,
      converter and calculator tools still run entirely on your device, and
      nothing you open or compute with them is sent anywhere, to us or to
      Google.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you would rather not be counted, any content blocker or the Google
      Analytics opt-out add-on will stop it, and the site works exactly the
      same without it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we still don't collect</h2>
    <p>
      No accounts, no sign-ins, no advertising or remarketing tags, and no
      selling or sharing of data with anyone beyond the analytics described
      above. We have no server that could receive your files, so we could not
      collect them even if we wanted to.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can go to the address on the
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
